const extraGrammar=[
['Countable and uncountable','Use many with countable plurals and much with uncountable nouns.','How ___ equipment do we need?','much','many','We bought many furniture.','We bought much furniture.','Describe what you need for a new apartment.'],
['Quantifiers','A few means some countable items; a little means some uncountable material.','There is ___ milk left.','a little','a few','I have a little books.','I have a few books.','Describe your available study resources.'],
['Comparatives','Use -er or more, followed by than.','This route is ___ than ours.','shorter','shortest','It is more easier.','It is easier.','Compare two ways of travelling.'],
['Superlatives','Use the with -est or most.','This is ___ option.','the cheapest','cheaper','She is most experienced student.','She is the most experienced student.','Describe the best place you have visited.'],
['Adverbs','Adverbs often modify verbs; adjectives modify nouns.','She explained the rule ___.','clearly','clear','He drives careful.','He drives carefully.','Explain how to perform a familiar task.'],
['Present Perfect vs Past Simple','Use Past Simple with finished past time; Present Perfect for experience or current relevance.','I ___ her yesterday.','met','have met','I have visited Rome last year.','I visited Rome last year.','Discuss a recent achievement and when it happened.'],
['Present Perfect Continuous','Have been + -ing emphasizes duration or ongoing activity.','She ___ for two hours and is still studying.','has been studying','studied','He has been work all day.','He has been working all day.','Describe something you have been learning.'],
['Past Perfect','Had + past participle marks an earlier past event.','By the time we arrived, the film ___.','had started','starts','She had went home.','She had gone home.','Describe a missed opportunity.'],
['Past Perfect Continuous','Had been + -ing emphasizes duration before a past point.','He was tired because he ___ all night.','had been working','works','They had been wait for hours.','They had been waiting for hours.','Explain why someone was exhausted.'],
['Future Continuous','Will be + -ing describes an action in progress at a future time.','At noon tomorrow I ___ to Paris.','will be flying','flew','I will be study at eight.','I will be studying at eight.','Describe your schedule tomorrow.'],
['Future Perfect','Will have + past participle marks completion by a future deadline.','By Friday we ___ the report.','will have finished','finish yesterday','She will have wrote it.','She will have written it.','Describe goals you expect to achieve next year.'],
['Zero Conditional','Use present forms in both clauses for general truths.','If water freezes, it ___.','expands','expanded','If you heat ice, it melt.','If you heat ice, it melts.','Explain a scientific principle.'],
['Third Conditional','If + had + participle, would have + participle describes an unreal past.','If we had left earlier, we ___ the train.','would have caught','will catch','If I had known, I would came.','If I had known, I would have come.','Discuss a decision you would change.'],
['Mixed Conditionals','A past condition can have a present hypothetical result.','If I had slept earlier, I ___ less tired now.','would be','would have been yesterday','If I had studied, I will know now.','If I had studied, I would know now.','Connect a past choice to your present situation.'],
['Passive Voice','Use be + past participle; tense is carried by be.','The bridge ___ in 1990.','was built','built','The results were publish.','The results were published.','Describe how a product is manufactured.'],
['Passive with Modals','Modal + be + past participle.','The form must ___ today.','be submitted','submitted','The issue should be solve.','The issue should be solved.','Explain rules for a laboratory.'],
['Reported Speech','Past reporting verbs often trigger backshift when reporting past statements.','She said she ___ tired at the time.','was','is being','He said that he can went.','He said that he could go.','Report a conversation you remember.'],
['Reported Questions','Use statement word order after the question word.','He asked where I ___.','lived','did live','She asked where was I.','She asked where I was.','Report questions from an interview.'],
['Relative Clauses','Who refers to people; which to things; that can introduce defining clauses.','The person ___ helped me was kind.','who','which','The book who I read was useful.','The book that I read was useful.','Describe a person who inspired you.'],
['Non-defining Relative Clauses','Use commas and who or which, not that, for supplementary information.','My bike, ___ is new, needs repair.','which','that','My sister, that lives abroad, called.','My sister, who lives abroad, called.','Describe a familiar place with extra details.'],
['Gerunds and Infinitives','Enjoy takes -ing; decide takes to + verb.','They decided ___ early.','to leave','leaving','I enjoy to swim.','I enjoy swimming.','Discuss activities you enjoy and plans you have.'],
['Verb Patterns','Some verbs change meaning with -ing or infinitive. Stop doing means cease an activity.','He stopped ___ because it was unhealthy.','smoking','to smoke','I avoid to drive at night.','I avoid driving at night.','Discuss a habit you changed.'],
['Modal Deduction','Must suggests strong inference; might possibility; cannot impossibility.','The lights are off; they ___ be asleep.','might','must to','She might knows the answer.','She might know the answer.','Infer what happened from clues.'],
['Past Modal Deduction','Modal + have + past participle expresses inference about the past.','The ground is wet; it might ___ overnight.','have rained','rained','He must have forgot.','He must have forgotten.','Explain a mysterious event.'],
['Wish and If Only','Wish + past form expresses an unreal present; past perfect expresses regret.','I wish I ___ more free time now.','had','have','I wish I can speak fluently.','I wish I could speak fluently.','Describe a change you wish for.'],
['Used to and Be Used to','Used to + verb describes past habits; be used to + noun or -ing describes familiarity.','I am used to ___ early.','waking up','wake up','She used to working here.','She used to work here.','Compare your current and past routines.'],
['Question Tags','A positive statement normally takes a negative tag and vice versa.','You know her, ___?','don’t you','do you','He is ready, does he?','He is ready, isn’t he?','Check information with a conversation partner.'],
['Indirect Questions','Use statement order in embedded questions.','Could you tell me where ___?','the station is','is the station','Do you know when does it start?','Do you know when it starts?','Ask politely for information.'],
['Concession and Contrast','Although introduces a clause; despite introduces a noun or -ing form.','___ the rain, we continued.','Despite','Although','Despite it was cold, we went out.','Although it was cold, we went out.','Discuss advantages despite drawbacks.'],
['Cause and Result','Because introduces a clause; because of introduces a noun phrase.','The flight was delayed ___ fog.','because of','because','We stayed home because of it rained.','We stayed home because it rained.','Explain the causes of a problem.'],
['Inversion','After negative fronted adverbials, invert auxiliary and subject.','Never ___ such a view.','have I seen','I have seen','Rarely we see this.','Rarely do we see this.','Describe an unusual experience.'],
['Participle Clauses','A participle clause normally shares its subject with the main clause.','___ the instructions, she began.','Having read','Have read','Walking home, the rain started.','Walking home, I noticed the rain starting.','Summarize a process using concise clauses.']
];
